text:
maria: FYI onboarding flagged confusing error surfaces in our sample apps. Users see raw HTTP text for 401/403/429 and TS/Go SDKs throw different shapes. Can we agree on a minimal cross-SDK error contract + retry hints?

ben: yep. Current mismatch: JS throws AuthError with code 'AUTH'; Go returns an http err string. No canonical code enum.

sophie: caused churn — a new user retried twice then gave up because sample app logged "request failed". We need both machine fields and a short human message.

alejandro: suggestion: API returns an error envelope and SDKs map to typed exceptions. Minimal envelope: { code, http_status, message, retryable, retry_after }. Example body: ```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED",
    "http_status": 429,
    "message": "quota exceeded for burst; try again",
    "retryable": true,
    "retry_after": 3
  }
}
```

maria: good. Questions: standardize code values? seconds vs header? opt-in compatibility?

ben: SDKs should instantiate native errors: e.g. TS `new RateLimitError(msg, { retryAfter: 3 })`, Go `type RateLimitError struct { Msg string; RetryAfter int }`. Keep code as canonical string for logs/alerts.

alejandro: servers should send both Retry-After header and body field. SDKs prefer body field when present, fallback to header.

ben: rollout plan: API add envelope; SDKs map behind minor flag; flip default after warning period. Back-compat for users parsing raw text.

sophie: add a short onboarding sample showing retry flow + docs blurb. That will cut support tickets.

maria: add concise human message and include KB link, e.g. "Invalid API key — check env var: https://redwood.ai/docs/errors#auth"

ben: sample snippet (TS): ```ts
try {
  await client.generate(...);
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof RateLimitError && err.retryAfter) {
    await sleep(err.retryAfter * 1000);
    // retry once
  }
  throw err;
}
```

alejandro: CI flagged sample-app lint fail when I added the wrapper.

